#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Performance Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde;, is used on a wide variety of computers by a wide variety of users. "
"Under the category of performance, this dialog box allows each user to "
"adjust options which may make the computer that &kde; is installed on feel "
"more responsive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "This module is divided into two tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "&konqueror; performance options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid "&konqueror; instances"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first section of this dialog is labeled <guilabel>Minimize Memory Usage</"
"guilabel> and has three options which determine maximum number of instances "
"of &konqueror; that can be open on one machine at any one time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do not confuse &konqueror; instances, with &konqueror; windows or tabs. The "
"number of konqueror instances is determined by &kde; not by the user. You "
"can think of instances as the hidden data of your &konqueror; windows and "
"tabs. One &konqueror; instance can contain the data for multiple windows or "
"tabs. Your choice on the following radio buttons does not limit the number "
"of windows you can open at one time, but rather, how many instances of "
"&konqueror; you can have open."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The reason the choices you make in this dialog box are important is evident "
"when something goes wrong and &konqueror; is forced to close an instance. "
"<emphasis>All &konqueror; windows associated with a &konqueror; instance "
"must be closed immediatly (without time to save data or bookmark locations)."
"</emphasis> Therefore, the more instances you can have open at one time, the "
"less likely a problem in one instance will affect all of your work. Each "
"instance requires more memory which can be a problem on systems with less "
"system memory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "Your options are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "Never"
msgstr "Jamai"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are no restraints. Any number of &konqueror; instances can be open at "
"any one time. The advantage of this option is if any &konqueror; instance "
"crashes the remaining will be unaffected. The disadvantage is that each "
"&konqueror; instance uses more memory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "For file browsing only (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, you can have as many as you want &konqueror; "
"instances open that are browsing the web, but only one instance of "
"&konqueror; for file management."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid "Always (use with care)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, you can only have one instance of &konqueror; "
"running at any one time. This saves system memory, but if your &konqueror; "
"window crashes, all your browsing windows close immediatly without warning. "
"This should only be used for seriously memory limited systems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "Preloading"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The subsection labeled <guilabel>Preloading</guilabel> also makes a tradeoff "
"between memory and performance."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Preloading</emphasis> refers to loading an instance of &konqueror; "
"into memory before a user asks to start &konqueror;. The positive effect of "
"this is that when a user asks &kde; to load &konqueror; the window appears "
"instantly because most of the application has been preloaded. The negative "
"effect is that this instance of &konqueror; uses memory that could be used "
"by other programs. By default, when a user closes &konqueror;, &kde; does "
"not close the instance. This means that the next time a user wants "
"&konqueror; loaded, it is nearly instantanous again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The spinbox labeled <guilabel>Maximum number of instances kept preloaded:</"
"guilabel> can be used to adjust the maximum number of preloaded instances. "
"This option does not affect instances when they are loaded. It also does not "
"limit the number of instances that can be used by active windows. It only "
"affects the number of preloaded instances."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The checkbox labeled <guilabel>Preload an instance after &kde; startup</"
"guilabel> does just what it says. It tells &kde; to preload one instance of "
"&konqueror; at the startup of &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "This does extend the startup time for &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The final checkbox labeled <guilabel>Always try to have at least one "
"preloaded instance</guilabel> signals to &kde; that you always want &kde; to "
"have one preloaded, but not used, instance of &konqueror; available. This "
"option will actually decrease performance on some machines (especially those "
"with limited physical memory)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde; system performance options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the tab labeled <guilabel>System</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Currently there is only one option labeled <guilabel>Disable system "
"configuration startup check</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &kde; starts, it checks several directories for changes to "
"configuration. Most of these changes relate to installation and uninstalling "
"applications to the computer. This scan extends the startup time for &kde; "
"and many times this scan is not needed as the configuration is current from "
"the last time &kde; was started. When the configuration has changed &kde; "
"uses this scan to update various datafiles to ensure a smooth user "
"experience."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are given the option to skip this initial scan during startup. &kde; "
"developers strongly suggest you do not disable this scan because of the "
"potential to introduce instability into your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you do select this option:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; will wait to perform the scan until after &kde; has started. This scan "
"will be performed after the desktop is loaded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the event of a crash, &kde; will not perform a backtrace because your "
"problem may be related to the delayed scan."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Switch this option off if any application is crashing as a delayed scan may "
"be responsible for the crash."
msgstr ""
